    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Vault denials",
      "description": "Audit responses carrying `permission denied`, reduced to the four things you want: operation, path, principal, source. `line_format` turns a 2 KB JSON record into one readable line \u2014 the full record is still there under the row expander.\n\nA denial is not automatically an attack; it is usually a policy boundary doing its job. The worked example in this deployment: `sys/generate-root/attempt` denied to `gcp-viaduct-controlplane`, because the CWE-863 remediation removed the admin policy's blanket `sys/*` grant. That is the control working \u2014 and is exactly what the `enable_unauthenticated_access = [\"generate-root\"]` listener setting was added to resolve. Denials on `auth/gcp/role/*` are the same story: admin deliberately cannot mint auth roles.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${DS_LOKI}"
          },
          "expr": "{node=~\"$node\", unit=\"vault.service\"} |= `permission denied` | json t=\"type\", path=\"request.path\", op=\"request.operation\", role=\"auth.metadata.role_name\", disp=\"auth.display_name\", addr=\"request.remote_address\" | t = `response` | label_format principal=\"{{ if .role }}{{ .role }}{{ else if .disp }}{{ .disp }}{{ else }}(unauthenticated){{ end }}\" | line_format \"DENIED  {{ .op }} {{ .path }}   principal={{ .principal }}  from={{ .addr }}\"",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
